WEBVTT

01:22.166 --> 01:24.585
Okay, okay, okay, okay...

01:26.962 --> 01:28.214
Okay...

02:05.417 --> 02:07.103
Yes... Yes...

02:07.127 --> 02:11.149
Yes, yes, come on...
Come on, yes! Yes, yes!

02:11.173 --> 02:13.175
Okay. Okay. Okay.

02:52.131 --> 02:54.133
Here we go, here we go.

02:54.717 --> 02:57.177
Okay. Okay. Fuck.

02:57.720 --> 03:00.180
Work. Work. Work.

03:01.348 --> 03:03.577
Standard... Okay...

03:03.601 --> 03:05.519
Standard, can you-
can you hear me?

03:06.604 --> 03:08.081
This is Naren.

03:08.105 --> 03:09.291
And I've, um...

03:09.315 --> 03:11.126
I've been separated,
uh, from the others.

03:11.150 --> 03:12.294
And I think I'm okay,

03:12.318 --> 03:13.777
but I'm not sure where I, uh...

03:14.361 --> 03:16.840
I've never been out
this far before, so I don't...

03:16.864 --> 03:18.091
Um...

03:18.115 --> 03:20.176
There was this, uh...

03:20.200 --> 03:22.286
I didn't get a good look
at it, but there was, um...

03:23.078 --> 03:24.705
there's something else in here.

03:26.999 --> 03:28.208
I need you guys.

03:28.751 --> 03:30.878
Okay? I need you guys
to get me, please.

03:32.046 --> 03:34.941
Fuck, I need you guys
to come out and get me.

03:34.965 --> 03:37.301
Can you... can you come,
please, standard?

03:38.010 --> 03:39.595
Standard?

03:40.930 --> 03:42.222
Oh, fuck!

03:46.393 --> 03:47.478
Fuck...

03:54.902 --> 03:56.612
Fuck! Fuck...

04:08.666 --> 04:10.250
Oh, shit... What the fuck?

05:42.593 --> 05:43.802
What the fuck?

06:07.993 --> 06:09.787
Fuck! Fuck! Fuck!

06:15.876 --> 06:16.960
Fuck!

06:20.756 --> 06:22.674
Fuck, fuck, fuck! Fuck!

07:49.052 --> 07:52.723
We all have
our loops, our habits...

07:55.434 --> 07:57.978
behaviors that keep us
walking in circles...

08:00.063 --> 08:01.708
reaching for the same solutions

08:01.732 --> 08:03.317
over and over again,

08:06.069 --> 08:08.864
thinking each time they'll
take you somewhere new.

08:09.990 --> 08:11.116
But they don't.

08:18.749 --> 08:19.934
And still,

08:19.958 --> 08:22.336
it's the neural pathway
of least resistance.

08:25.631 --> 08:27.424
A path you made.

08:28.091 --> 08:29.819
It's the one that kept you safe

08:29.843 --> 08:31.220
when you were a child.

08:36.767 --> 08:38.560
You learned to push people away

08:39.144 --> 08:40.604
before they could hurt you.

08:43.065 --> 08:44.250
And now,

08:44.274 --> 08:45.418
as an adult,

08:45.442 --> 08:47.694
you're still stuck
right where you started.

08:53.325 --> 08:54.409
Alone.

09:00.666 --> 09:02.167
I mean, I'm not lonely.

09:03.085 --> 09:07.398
I have employees
and... customers.

09:07.422 --> 09:10.050
I didn't say lonely.
I said alone.

09:10.759 --> 09:12.302
Yeah, well, I mean...

09:14.429 --> 09:15.949
I hurt people.

09:15.973 --> 09:17.951
I don't want to.
It's just the way I'm wired.

09:17.975 --> 09:19.935
So maybe I deserve to be alone.

09:20.769 --> 09:22.980
Do you think anyone
deserves to be alone?

09:24.064 --> 09:25.875
I don't know, but, you know,

09:25.899 --> 09:27.567
maybe it's not such a bad thing.

09:28.527 --> 09:30.338
Being alone feels...

09:30.362 --> 09:31.613
deeply ingrained.

09:32.155 --> 09:33.240
I understand.

09:34.116 --> 09:37.136
You've had dreams
and a lot of resistance,

09:37.160 --> 09:40.807
not a lot of support
in realizing those dreams.

09:40.831 --> 09:43.625
And when we've experienced...

09:44.418 --> 09:47.212
hurt again and again,

09:47.713 --> 09:49.065
we start to expect it.

09:49.089 --> 09:50.608
It's like,
"Oh, I know this path.

09:50.632 --> 09:51.925
I know where it goes."

09:53.510 --> 09:54.553
So...

09:55.470 --> 09:58.116
are you interested
in forging a new path

09:58.140 --> 09:59.308
and see where that leads?

09:59.933 --> 10:03.061
Sure. Why not?
You know, I'm here.

10:04.104 --> 10:05.147
Great.

10:05.647 --> 10:07.083
So I want to revisit

10:07.107 --> 10:09.401
an exercise we've done before.

10:10.777 --> 10:11.796
The role play.

10:11.820 --> 10:13.423
-Oh, the acting thing?
-Yeah.

10:13.447 --> 10:15.425
-I feel stupid doing that.
-I know.

10:15.449 --> 10:17.868
But we have a few minutes.
Let's, um...

10:18.785 --> 10:20.662
Yeah, let's try. A little bit.

10:21.163 --> 10:22.539
All right.

10:23.123 --> 10:24.458
Let's set the scene.

10:25.125 --> 10:29.629
Let's go back to the night
that Barbara left you.

10:30.547 --> 10:32.150
You mean the night
she kicked me out

10:32.174 --> 10:33.300
of my own house?

10:33.842 --> 10:35.093
Yeah.

10:35.677 --> 10:36.845
I'm playing myself.

10:37.346 --> 10:40.015
-And I'll be Barbara.
-It is my house, by the way.

10:40.766 --> 10:42.309
I'm the one paying for it.

10:42.809 --> 10:45.228
-I know.
-All right.

10:47.773 --> 10:49.399
Okay, so, um...

10:50.859 --> 10:53.087
I got home late.
I don't know how late.

10:53.111 --> 10:55.572
Uh... She was already asleep.
Maybe midnight.

10:56.698 --> 10:58.634
She usually goes to bed
before... It doesn't matter.

10:58.658 --> 11:01.512
The point is, I was
in the kitchen, and, um...

11:01.536 --> 11:03.598
the glass, I broke the glass,

11:03.622 --> 11:07.793
and she comes running down
to see what happened, and...

11:08.418 --> 11:09.812
things escalated.

11:09.836 --> 11:11.171
And how do you feel?

11:12.047 --> 11:13.858
Well, I was...

11:13.882 --> 11:16.652
I was drunk, and, um...

11:16.676 --> 11:18.571
I-I felt stupid, you know.

11:18.595 --> 11:21.866
I was angry, because...
because I broke the glass.

11:21.890 --> 11:23.159
Can you say that to me?

11:23.183 --> 11:25.560
-Uh, what, to-to Barbara?
-Yeah.

11:28.397 --> 11:31.900
Um... I'm sorry that I woke you.

11:34.820 --> 11:37.382
Maybe if you'd
come home earlier,

11:37.406 --> 11:39.408
we could have spent
the evening together.

11:40.450 --> 11:42.220
No, I was...
I was working, you know?

11:42.244 --> 11:44.055
I came straight home after work.

11:44.079 --> 11:45.789
Be honest with me, please.

11:46.581 --> 11:48.333
I can smell it on your breath.

11:50.919 --> 11:52.129
I had a few beers.

11:52.504 --> 11:53.898
Define a few.

11:53.922 --> 11:55.298
Well, it was a hard day.

11:56.425 --> 11:57.610
I needed to wind down.

11:57.634 --> 11:59.344
All you ever do is wind down.

12:00.178 --> 12:01.555
You're always at the store.

12:06.017 --> 12:07.394
You want kids, right?

12:08.895 --> 12:10.706
-We both do.
-Well, you know...

12:10.730 --> 12:11.999
having a family takes money,

12:12.023 --> 12:13.608
which means someone has to work.

12:14.234 --> 12:16.045
Unless being
a professional student

12:16.069 --> 12:17.755
is considered a job these days.

12:17.779 --> 12:19.924
That's not fair. You know
I had to take time off.

12:19.948 --> 12:21.759
Well, it's not my fault
if you can't keep up.

12:21.783 --> 12:23.010
How are you going to be a lawyer

12:23.034 --> 12:24.661
if you can't even handle
law school?

12:26.163 --> 12:27.682
Who do you think pays
for everything

12:27.706 --> 12:29.392
while you're gallivanting
around campus

12:29.416 --> 12:30.834
like a 30-year-old freshman?

12:31.418 --> 12:33.128
I'll give you a hint: it's me.

12:33.879 --> 12:36.232
I pay for your school, I pay
for your time off school,

12:36.256 --> 12:37.567
I pay for the roof
over your head.

12:37.591 --> 12:38.985
-Can I talk now?
-No! No.

12:39.009 --> 12:40.945
Because I'd like to know,
what do you think happens

12:40.969 --> 12:42.363
if you do manage to graduate?

12:42.387 --> 12:44.615
You know, you pop out a kid,
then leave me with the bill.

12:44.639 --> 12:47.660
Or am I stuck
at home changing diapers because

12:47.684 --> 12:49.787
you're too busy working for
the first time in your life?

12:49.811 --> 12:52.022
-Now you're being cruel.
-I'm being honest.

12:52.898 --> 12:54.608
I thought that's
what you always wanted.

12:55.692 --> 12:58.087
Just because you didn't get to
be an architect doesn't mean...

12:58.111 --> 12:59.654
I am a fucking architect!

13:00.864 --> 13:03.718
God damn it, I'm just stuck
selling shit furniture because

13:03.742 --> 13:06.745
someone won't get off their
fat fucking ass and help me!

13:15.045 --> 13:16.421
How do you feel, Clark?

13:22.010 --> 13:23.446
Who am I talking to?

13:23.470 --> 13:25.138
-Me, here, now.
-You? Okay.

13:26.806 --> 13:27.849
Um...

13:29.017 --> 13:31.037
I'm sorry,
I didn't mean to, uh...

13:31.061 --> 13:33.498
you know, get angry

13:33.522 --> 13:35.708
or lose my temper or whatever.

13:35.732 --> 13:36.733
I know.

13:37.359 --> 13:39.903
That's the purpose
of the whole exercise.

13:40.946 --> 13:42.197
This is a good start.

13:42.822 --> 13:44.342
To feel what you feel,

13:44.366 --> 13:46.868
and then learn to identify
a new path.

13:47.911 --> 13:51.164
Your reaction was
actually quite normal.

13:53.875 --> 13:55.001
Well, that's me!

13:56.378 --> 13:58.981
Well, ahoy there, mateys!

13:59.005 --> 14:01.275
Tired of spending
your hard-earned doubloons

14:01.299 --> 14:02.944
on overpriced furniture?

14:02.968 --> 14:05.905
Looking for deals
that'll shiver your timbers?

14:05.929 --> 14:07.406
Then come on down

14:07.430 --> 14:09.700
to Cap'n Clark's Ottoman Empire,

14:09.724 --> 14:11.160
the Santa Clara Valley's

14:11.184 --> 14:13.412
favorite warehouse
and showrooms.

14:13.436 --> 14:15.498
You'll find bedrooms,
living rooms,

14:15.522 --> 14:18.501
dinettes, dens
and bathrooms aplenty.

14:18.525 --> 14:21.045
First-time homeowners?
We've got ya.

14:21.069 --> 14:23.548
New parents looking
for Billy's first crib?

14:23.572 --> 14:24.715
We've got ya!

14:24.739 --> 14:26.551
From the latest in modern design

14:26.575 --> 14:28.803
to the classic styles
of yesteryear,

14:28.827 --> 14:31.496
it's all here
and it's all a steal.

14:32.038 --> 14:33.307
What's that, Polly?

14:33.331 --> 14:34.725
You're worried about credit?

14:34.749 --> 14:38.771
Ha! Cap'n Clark says
no credit, no problem!

14:38.795 --> 14:40.940
Sail the high seas
of high quality,

14:40.964 --> 14:43.568
and leave your money problems
at the door.

14:43.592 --> 14:44.694
Walk in today

14:44.718 --> 14:46.571
and get your dream
sectional lounger,

14:46.595 --> 14:49.865
kitchen table, floor lamp,
and bed frame here

14:49.889 --> 14:52.410
at Cap'n Clark's Ottoman Empire,

14:52.434 --> 14:56.038
located at Capitol and McKee,
just off the 680.

14:56.062 --> 14:58.023
Arr! Walk in today...

14:59.065 --> 15:00.251
kick your feet back,

15:00.275 --> 15:02.670
and enjoy an empire of your own!

15:02.694 --> 15:05.089
For every sultan
deserves a throne,

15:05.113 --> 15:07.174
and we've got one
with your name on it,

15:07.198 --> 15:08.533
here at Cap'n Clark's...

15:09.909 --> 15:10.909
No way!

15:11.286 --> 15:13.014
-Clark, you good?
-Turn the camera off.

15:13.038 --> 15:14.807
No, no, it's good.
It's outtake stuff, dude.

15:14.831 --> 15:17.042
-Turn the fucking camera off.
-Okay... Jesus...

15:19.502 --> 15:20.688
You, uh, you need help?

15:20.712 --> 15:22.881
No, I got it, I got it.

15:23.923 --> 15:24.900
Um...

15:24.924 --> 15:26.944
-Are we going again, or...?
-No.

15:26.968 --> 15:28.779
Kat, you can open the store now.

15:28.803 --> 15:30.930
We've been open.

15:33.266 --> 15:35.536
You know, dude,
I still don't get it.

15:35.560 --> 15:38.414
Are you, like,
a pirate or a sultan?

15:38.438 --> 15:40.916
-Just be good to establish it.
-I'm a... Shut up.

15:40.940 --> 15:44.235
Piece of cheap
particleboard bullshit.

15:44.944 --> 15:46.738
Clear this stuff up, will you?

15:47.656 --> 15:48.740
Here.

16:06.758 --> 16:07.842
Sorry about that.

16:08.635 --> 16:09.695
How's it looking?

16:09.719 --> 16:11.280
Meter reads fine.

16:11.304 --> 16:13.682
If your bill's coming in high,
that's on you.

16:14.724 --> 16:16.893
What about the outages?
That happens after hours.

16:17.686 --> 16:21.064
Don't know. Fluorescents
must be tripping a breaker.

16:22.190 --> 16:25.461
I turn the overheads off
when the store closes,

16:25.485 --> 16:26.903
before the power gets weird.

16:27.570 --> 16:29.656
Anyway, wouldn't that
just make the bills go down?

16:32.909 --> 16:34.202
Where's your breaker box?

16:35.704 --> 16:36.972
I'm no expert,

16:36.996 --> 16:39.767
but I checked earlier,
and everything looks okay.

16:39.791 --> 16:42.144
-You said the lights flicker.
-Yeah, the whole store does.

16:42.168 --> 16:43.896
-Huh.
-Just not at the same time.

16:43.920 --> 16:45.272
One night,
I lose the power upstairs.

16:45.296 --> 16:48.425
Next night, it's down here.
There's no rhyme or...

16:55.432 --> 16:57.183
Who the hell installed
this thing?

16:57.934 --> 16:59.537
Well, the building came wired.

16:59.561 --> 17:01.604
I mean, it's dated,
but it's not that old.

17:08.319 --> 17:09.654
Take a look at this.

17:14.033 --> 17:15.410
That wasn't there before.

17:15.910 --> 17:20.433
Or... maybe I didn't notice.
Like I say, I'm no expert.

17:20.457 --> 17:22.393
Why-why is it...
why is it going that way?

17:22.417 --> 17:24.794
Better question:

17:25.628 --> 17:27.505
what is it even connected to?

17:28.798 --> 17:29.883
Huh?

17:37.098 --> 17:39.559
CLARK Kat! How's the power?

17:40.477 --> 17:41.537
What?

17:41.561 --> 17:43.313
Anything happen up there?

17:43.855 --> 17:45.124
Damn...

17:45.148 --> 17:46.232
The rat's back.

17:46.816 --> 17:48.502
-But the power's on.
-Yeah.

17:48.526 --> 17:50.254
I thought we killed the rat.

17:50.278 --> 17:51.404
We killed a rat.

17:52.989 --> 17:55.384
-So is this the problem?
-Don't see how.

17:55.408 --> 17:57.786
Power can't even go through
this part of the circuit.

17:58.244 --> 17:59.430
It's just...

17:59.454 --> 18:00.455
there.

18:01.080 --> 18:03.476
Like some schmo
just stuck it in there.

18:03.500 --> 18:06.044
Yeah.

18:14.469 --> 18:15.780
MAN 1 Do you ever feel

18:15.804 --> 18:17.698
like you're living behind glass?

18:17.722 --> 18:19.140
Watching life happen,

18:19.724 --> 18:22.060
but never really
stepping into it?

18:22.811 --> 18:26.356
Maybe it's time
to open the window within.

18:27.065 --> 18:29.502
You can be
the author of your own design

18:29.526 --> 18:31.587
because we all deserve
another chance

18:31.611 --> 18:32.987
to fulfill our dreams.

18:33.696 --> 18:35.841
The moment you believe
change is possible,

18:35.865 --> 18:37.242
you've already begun.

18:37.826 --> 18:39.512
MAN 1 Order The Window Within

18:39.536 --> 18:41.931
and the companion
three-part audio program,

18:41.955 --> 18:45.142
Guided Openings,
by Dr. Mary Klein.

18:45.166 --> 18:48.086
Available now
for $24.95 plus shipping.

18:48.920 --> 18:53.341
Call 1-800-555-0199.

18:54.342 --> 18:57.303
It's never
too late to forge a new path.

18:59.264 --> 19:01.367
So, you're
still trusting paper folders,

19:01.391 --> 19:03.953
mislabeled tapes,
and a locked filing cabinet

19:03.977 --> 19:05.621
that anyone
with a spare key can open?

19:05.645 --> 19:07.623
Your business runs
on information,

19:07.647 --> 19:10.900
yet most companies treat
their data like clutter...

19:14.445 --> 19:16.674
That small blip
is not an asteroid.

19:16.698 --> 19:18.634
It's a spaceship,
and it's on our tail.

19:18.658 --> 19:21.053
-It's getting closer.
-Impossible, Rigna.

19:21.077 --> 19:23.722
They couldn't have spotted us.
We have our radar shield on.

19:23.746 --> 19:26.308
I know that, sir,
but they are gaining on us.

19:26.332 --> 19:28.477
Is it possible
Earth has a secret device

19:28.501 --> 19:30.545
that can penetrate
our radar shield?

20:06.623 --> 20:08.166
Piece of shit.

20:54.837 --> 20:58.341
Why did you do this to yourself?

21:02.011 --> 21:03.513
How did you get here?

21:06.808 --> 21:10.829
Your consciousness
is a room full of memories

21:10.853 --> 21:13.439
that is constantly evolving.

21:15.441 --> 21:17.026
But as you walk through life,

21:17.777 --> 21:20.947
the untrained mind
can start to build walls,

21:22.240 --> 21:23.574
put up barriers

21:24.659 --> 21:26.995
to protect itself
from the outside world.

21:28.621 --> 21:30.373
It's a natural response.

21:31.374 --> 21:33.710
Something we are
often unaware of.

21:34.794 --> 21:36.522
But if gone unchecked,

21:36.546 --> 21:38.423
it can leave you
feeling trapped.

21:40.174 --> 21:42.528
You can become convinced
that the world outside

21:42.552 --> 21:44.303
is better off without you.

21:45.138 --> 21:47.640
That you never deserve
the relationships you've had.

21:48.641 --> 21:51.203
Resigned to watch
your life unfold

21:51.227 --> 21:53.187
from behind a lone window.

21:55.481 --> 21:57.358
I can help you open it now

21:58.818 --> 22:00.820
because the window isn't locked.

22:02.822 --> 22:05.033
The latch was never broken.

22:08.077 --> 22:10.204
Are you ready to step through?

22:12.582 --> 22:15.960
So that you can reclaim that
which was once yours...

22:17.378 --> 22:20.506
and take back control
of your life.

22:22.133 --> 22:24.052
The life you want to be living.

22:25.762 --> 22:28.473
Unburdened by the traumas of the past.

22:29.348 --> 22:32.036
Free of the confines
you had built.

22:32.060 --> 22:33.704
To leave, and so I decided...

22:33.728 --> 22:37.523
And free to choose
a path of your own design.

23:13.559 --> 23:16.246
Well, hey there,
cowboys and cowgirls!

23:16.270 --> 23:18.082
Are you looking
to rustle up the best deals

23:18.106 --> 23:19.291
this side of the Rio Grande?

23:19.315 --> 23:20.334
Prick.

23:20.358 --> 23:23.128
Well, yeehaw, I say yeehaw!

23:23.152 --> 23:25.172
Here at Big Wayne's,
our dining room sets

23:25.196 --> 23:27.758
are gonna make you feel
like you just struck gold.

23:27.782 --> 23:30.219
So don't even think
about going anyplace else.

23:30.243 --> 23:32.954
Big Wayne's,
just look for the golden...

23:48.427 --> 23:49.554
What the...

24:06.487 --> 24:09.907
Stupid... Fuck! Piece of shit!

29:49.330 --> 29:51.016
Gok wai hou maa?

29:51.040 --> 29:53.083
Zuk gok wai ping on gin
Hong faai lok.

29:56.045 --> 29:59.507
Zdrávstvuyte! Privétstvuyu Vas!

30:15.981 --> 30:18.192
Bonjour tout le monde.

30:19.151 --> 30:21.111
Naykaungg parsalarr?

30:22.696 --> 30:23.989
Shalom.

30:24.532 --> 30:26.951
Hola y saludos a todos.

30:27.993 --> 30:29.930
Selamat malam hadirin sekalian,

30:29.954 --> 30:31.431
selamat berpisah...

30:31.455 --> 30:32.432
Hello?

30:32.456 --> 30:33.725
Dilain waktu.

30:33.749 --> 30:36.311
Kay pachamamta niytapas may tap as

30:36.335 --> 30:38.647
rimapallasta runasimipi.

30:38.671 --> 30:40.339
Aao ji, jee aya nu.

30:45.302 --> 30:47.781
Salvete quicumque estis;

30:47.805 --> 30:50.951
bonam erga
vos voluntatem habemus,

30:50.975 --> 30:53.811
et pacem per astra ferimus.

30:55.980 --> 30:58.333
Hartelijke groeten aan iedereen.

30:58.357 --> 31:00.568
Herzliche Grüße an alle.

31:01.485 --> 31:03.380
Assalamu alaikum.

31:03.404 --> 31:07.425
Hum zameen ke rehne
waalon ki taraf se

31:07.449 --> 31:10.387
